// Window placement for streaming. The capture output's own config lives in
// stream-output.kdl, which Sunshine rewrites per session.
//
// Was: Included AFTER dms/outputs.kdl in config.kdl so these win
// over DMS's auto-generated blocks — the same last-wins ordering binds.kdl uses.
//
// HDMI-A-1 (plateau) is a 4K EDID dongle, not a display: Sunshine captures it
// so every Moonlight client streams at its own resolution without retiming the
// desktop monitor. Off by default so it isn't a phantom workspace windows can
// wander onto; mySunshine.captureOutput's prep-cmd turns it on, sets the
// client's mode, and turns it back off when the stream ends.
//
// Inert on hosts that have no such output (rhizome), so this stays host-neutral.

// Window placement during a stream. focus-monitor in Sunshine's prep-cmd is
// only advisory: Steam maps its windows whenever it feels like it and restores
// them to their last-used monitor, so games landed on DP-3 at random.
//
// This is deterministic instead. open-on-output resolves against niri's set of
// MAPPED outputs (global_space.outputs() in handlers/xdg_shell.rs), and a
// disabled output is not in that set — so while HDMI-A-1 is off, which is its
// normal state, the lookup fails and placement falls through to the focused
// monitor exactly as before. The rule only bites while Sunshine has the dongle
// up, which is precisely when every new window belongs on it.
//
// Scoped to Steam deliberately, NOT a catch-all. niri consults open-on-output
// BEFORE a window's own fullscreen output request (handlers/xdg_shell.rs), so a
// catch-all intercepts games that open by asking to be fullscreen on a given
// output — they came up windowed. Steam has no such preference at open, so
// pinning it here is safe, and games inherit the dongle from focus-monitor in
// Sunshine's prep-cmd while keeping their fullscreen path intact.
window-rule {
    match app-id="steam"
    open-on-output "HDMI-A-1"
}
